    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78441" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμῡθ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>consolatory</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μυθητικὸν ὁ φίλος καὶ τῇ ὄψει καὶ
					τῷ λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1171b2
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>able to assuage</i> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν
				ἑαυτοῦ παθῶν</span>), Chrysipp. ap. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.70
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λόγος</span> a letter <i>of
				consolation</i>, such as <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i> wrote to Apollonius, <i><span class="en">
				2.101e
			</span></i> sq.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὑπόληψις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					12.40
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>
			<i>consolation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				6.4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					225.41
				</span></i>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.622
			</span></i>.</div>
